ction with acute decompensation: less likely due to sudden onset and hemodynamic instability", "Exertional rhabdomyolysis with systemic complications: unlikely as primary explanation without CK elevation", "Ovarian pathology (e.g., torsion, abscess): could explain RUQ pain but doesn't account for hemodynamic collapse"], "alarm_features": ["Hypotension (BP 80/40 mmHg)", "Tachycardia (pulse 110/minute)", "Temperature 37.5°C"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Gynecologic / Pelvic Source of Acute Hemodynamic Instability and RUQ Pain", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.4761904761904762, "posterior": 0.36527545847285037, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["The subacute presentation with constitutional symptoms and hemodynamic instability is consistent with gynecologic sepsis (e.g., ruptured abscess), moderately s…"], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.95, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "anatomy", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Hepatic / Hepatobiliary Vascular Source of Acute Hemodynamic Instability and RUQ Pain", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.28571428571428575, "posterior": 0.1366223228399246, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Chronic alcohol use is a known risk factor for Budd-Chiari syndrome, but the absence of jaundice/ascites in the physical exam creates uncertainty, resulting in…"], "evidence_against": ["The absence of classical Budd-Chiari signs (jaundice, hepatomegaly) weakens this diagnosis despite alcohol risk factors."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1", "B2.2"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.75, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "anatomy", "representative_diseases": []}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Biliary Obstruction with Secondary Hemodynamic Compromise", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.053, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Lack of biliary risk factors substantially reduces the probability of biliary obstruction as the primary cause."]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Pancreatic Source of Acute Hemodynamic Instability and RUQ Pain", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.053, "danger": 0.75, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The absence of both typical pain pattern and pending enzymatic confirmation strongly argues against pancreatitis as the primary cause."]}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Hepatic Vascular Ectasia with Hemodynamic Instability", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.013, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["These physical signs are more consistent with Cushing's syndrome than with hepatic vascular ectasia, but Cushing's is not currently a considered branch."]}, "B1.1": {"id": "B1.1", "label": "Ectopic Pregnancy with Hemoperitoneum and Hemodynamic Instability", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.342, "danger": 0.9, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The absence of a missed period or vaginal bleeding slightly reduces the probability of ectopic pregnancy, though β-hCG results remain pending."]}, "B1.2": {"id": "B1.2", "label": "Ruptured Ovarian Abscess with Septic Shock", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.024, "danger": 0.85, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Cushing’s features are more suggestive of hormonal pathology than sepsis, further weakening the ruptured ovarian abscess hypothesis."]}, "B1.3": {"id": "B1.3", "label": "Septic Abortion with Hemodynamic Instability",